  "body": "Fork synced at v0.18.0 (cut from upstream/main 0757563d).\n\n## What changed\n\nThe posed sweep of fixture laws (c2)/(d2) (`crates/sim/src/verify/posed_steel.rs`) placed each band of a leaning tool stack as a capsule. A capsule's caps reach one whole band radius past each band end, so an r 15 holder standing 0.5 mm over a clamp was convicted `FixtureHit` at any lean at all.\n\nA box the capsule reaches is now read a second time against the band as the flat-ended cylinder it is (`flat_band_clear`):\n\n- per interval: the tip chord `p0..p1` swept exactly + the cylinder `lo..hi`, radius `r`, about the midpoint pose + a ball of `pad = bulge + swing * hypot(max(|lo|,|hi|), r)`;\n- fixed steel under a rotary: that set carried by the midpoint turn and grown by `dth * (rho_max + r + pad)`, `rho_max` over the parallelogram's four corners;\n- cleared only on a GJK proof of a separating plane wider than `pad + FIXTURE_HIT_TOL` (`fixture_mesh::band_clear_of_box`: the mesh law's existing `SweptBand`/`Boxed` supports and `gjk::separated`, pointed at a fixture box).\n\nThis is the enclosure `verify/mesh_posed.rs` already proves for the fixture mesh law; the box law now reads the same geometry. Leaning by θ the rim reaches R sin θ past the end plane, not R, and the verdict turns at the lean where the true band touches.\n\n## Why it is still conservative\n\n- Both enclosures contain the swept band (proof in the module header and in `docs/decisions/1305-posed-band-cylinder.md`); a box is struck only when both reach it, so nothing the true band touches can be cleared.\n- The cylinder's swing arm is `hypot(hi, r)` (the rim's distance from the tip), not the capsule's centreline arm `|hi|`.\n- \"Clear\" is only the supporting-hyperplane bound over exact support mappings. Non-finite input, a zero axis, a degenerate rotary or an exhausted search is \"not proven\": the capsule's hit stands.\n- Every verdict that was clear is clear by the same arithmetic (the capsule still runs first); only capsule hits can change. No golden moved.\n\n## Tests\n\nNew, `crates/sim/src/verify/posed_steel_tests.rs` (unit, on `posed_hits` / `sweep`):\n\n- `a_holder_just_over_a_clamp_is_clear_at_a_small_real_lean` - the issue's evidence case (r 15 holder, clamp top 0.5 mm under it): clear from 1e-7 to 1.5 degrees (0.01 degrees included).\n- `the_holder_is_struck_once_its_rim_really_reaches_the_clamp` - convicted as `Holder` from 2.2 degrees.\n- `the_verdict_turns_once_and_at_the_true_touching_lean` - 1000 leans, 0.005 to 5 degrees: the verdict flips exactly once, within 0.006 degrees of the analytic touching lean (2.130 degrees).\n- `a_fixed_clamp_under_the_stood_up_holder_is_clear_at_any_lean` - machine frame, clear at 29.5 and struck at 30.5.\n- `steel_at_any_point_of_the_true_leaning_band_is_struck` - the property: 4800 specks of steel at sampled points of the true band (rims and end faces weighted) on moves whose pose swings, path frame and under a rotary, all struck.\n- `a_non_finite_band_or_box_is_never_proven_clear`.\n\nNew, `crates/sim/tests/posed_band_cylinder.rs` (public laws): fixed clamp under a rotary clear at any lean / convicted when it reaches into the holder (`bands_vs_workholding`, `rapids_vs_workholding`); a 5 degree lean still convicts through `bands_vs_fixtures`.\n\nMutation checks (not committed): dropping the swing term from `pad` fails the property test; removing the second reading fails the three clearance tests.\n\n## Gate (final head e15b633e)\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: green - sim suites (lib + 20 binaries, `posed_band_cylinder` among them), motion (`real_tip`, `solid_law`), app (46 binaries); 3 steps, 0 failed, 3.4 min.\n- By hand: `posed_fixture` 7/7, `posed_fixture_midpose` 3/3, `stock_posed` 3/3, `fixture_mesh` 9/9 (1 ignored, release lane).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-sim -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Not exercised / known limits\n\n- **`main` has neither #938 nor #1303.** PR #973 (`UPRIGHT_TILT_RAD`) is open and #1303 is open with no branch pushed, so this is built on `upstream/main` alone and `crates/sim/tests/tilt_tolerance.rs` does not exist here. In the path frame, law (c2) also runs its own column enclosure (`stack_span::band_struck`), which still drops a leaning band by its whole radius - that is #1303. Until it merges, `bands_vs_fixtures` on the evidence case is still convicted at 0.01 degrees by the column, not by the sweep. The sweep's verdict is pinned directly, and end to end where the sweep alone decides (fixed steel under a rotary).\n- PR #973 changes one line of `posed_steel.rs` (`is_vertical` -> `is_upright`), away from these hunks; whichever merges second should merge cleanly.\n- A move whose pose CHANGES keeps the swing ball (`swing * hypot(hi, r)`, intervals of 0.5 mm of far-end travel): continuous, but wider than a constant-pose move's reading.\n- `mesh_posed.rs` already sweeps flat-ended bands (read in full). `probe.rs` was skimmed, not audited; unchanged.\n- No release-lane (`--ignored`) suites were run.\n\nChangelog: The posed fixture sweep reads each band of a leaning tool as the flat-ended cylinder it is, so a holder just over a clamp is no longer reported as a fixture hit at a small tilt (#1305)\n\nEffort: max (no escalation)\n\nFixes #1305\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
